50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have our candidates: the Microbiome Atlas, Plant Drought Signaling, Protein Folding Dynamics, and Regeneration in Amphibians.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The Atlas sounds lovely, but I wonder if the others are more feasible given the current costs.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,The glasshouses are full! That makes the Plant Drought project sound really difficult right now.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"And the Amphibian project relies on breeding colonies, which my research suggests are prone to schedule overruns.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,The Microbiome Atlas is a catalogue. Those tend to be the most enduring and successful investments.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"The Protein Folding project needs modelling, and we have a surplus of those technicians. That is a strong point.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Midori,,"But the Atlas also uses computing, which is currently free. It seems very cost-effective.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"But wait, the Protein Folding project needs spectroscopy, and that equipment has been unreliable!","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A valid point, Kenji. The Atlas avoids the breeding risks and the spectroscopy failures.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It also benefits from the faster repository turnaround for its sequences.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I am inclined toward the Atlas or the Protein project, but the lack of phenotyping staff hurts the others.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Midori,,I think the Atlas provides the best balance and harmony for the current funding climate.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I agree! Let's go with the Atlas since the glasshouses and spectroscopy are such a mess!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The logic holds. The Atlas minimizes the most volatile risks we've identified.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I concur. It is the most reliable choice.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Servas,,Then we are in agreement. Let us cast our votes.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Midori,,Ready.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Kenji,,Me too!,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Ready.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
